# Telecom Customer Churn Analysis & Prediction

## 📌 Project Overview
This project focuses on analyzing and predicting customer churn in the telecom industry using machine learning and business intelligence techniques. The objective is to identify high-risk customers and provide actionable insights to improve customer retention.

---

## 🎯 Objectives
- Analyze customer behavior and churn patterns in telecom data
- Build a machine learning model to predict customer churn
- Identify key factors influencing churn using explainable AI techniques
- Visualize insights through an interactive Power BI dashboard

---

## 🛠️ Tools & Technologies
- Python (Pandas, NumPy, Scikit-learn)
- Machine Learning (Logistic Regression, Random Forest)
- Class Imbalance Handling (SMOTE)
- Model Explainability (SHAP)
- Power BI (Interactive Dashboard)
- Google Colab (Development Environment)

---

## 📊 Key Features
- Data cleaning and exploratory data analysis (EDA)
- Feature engineering and preprocessing
- Churn prediction using Random Forest classifier
- SHAP-based explainability to identify churn drivers
- Customer risk segmentation (Low, Medium, High Risk)
- Interactive Power BI dashboard with KPIs and insights

---

## 📈 Key Insights
- Customers on month-to-month contracts show the highest churn rate
- Low tenure customers are more likely to churn
- Higher monthly charges significantly increase churn probability
- Fiber optic internet service users exhibit higher churn risk

---

## 📌 Deliverables
- Jupyter Notebook containing the complete analysis and model implementation
- CSV file with churn predictions and customer risk levels
- Power BI dashboard and PDF export for visualization and reporting

---

## 🚀 Outcome
This project enables telecom companies to proactively identify customers likely to churn and supports data-driven strategies for customer retention.

